{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And an earthen vessel that he touches.</b> It says here 'in it' and it says below 'in which it is cooked' — just as the 'in it' stated below refers to its interior airspace, so too the 'in it' stated here refers to its interior airspace. And since we have learned that a zav does not defile it except through its airspace, what does Scripture mean by <b>that he touches</b>? To teach you what kind of touch is equivalent to the whole of it — you would say this is moving it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:24.617494471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}